ains enforcing. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state was captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, and service, content, SELinux policy, firewall state, and listener recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The application request was made from node1 to its own node IP rather than from a separate external client, although the all-interface listener and active runtime/permanent firewall rule strongly support network availability.","The lifecycle snapshots do not directly inventory SELinux mode, firewall rules, application files, or installed packages; those final states are instead established by executor commands."]}
